  "pass_a_gloss": "Souls of the righteous enter; the regions of death no longer take the spirits of the living. With you, beginning of the living and made at the same time of the dead, that you may rule over the dead and the living, all of the dead are bold, not by word, the flock. 'Receive then my spirit.' Do not allow your sparrow to be lured by those hunting or by those meeting at the gates of enemies to plunder my exile from the earth or to disturb my ascent into the heavens. But this one he offered for himself the prayer, another again for the people of the Jews; 'Lord, do not set this sin upon them.' And\nbecoming\nregions of the living\nthe your sparrow\nBut this one indeed\nnot outside of reason\nthe foam\nthe food,\nnot outside word\nnot outside word'\nnot anymore the gloomy things of death realms the of living receives spirits\nin order that also of dead and of living you may rule\ntakes to oneself\nterrible of the death\nNot permit the thine sparrow to bring forth\nnot anymore the terrible of the death separate the of the living things spirits receive\nNot permit the thine sparrow to bring forth...\nAfter you firstfruit of the living and the dead having become together\nsouls of the just enter in\nno longer the dark places of death\nthe places of the living\nit takes/accepts spirits/winds\nit receives spirits\nsouls of the just enter the no longer dark places of death receive spirits\ndo not consent your sparrow to lie in wait to the hunters",
  "pass_b_english": [
    "The souls of the righteous enter; the gloomy regions of death no longer receive the spirits of the living.",
    "After you, the firstfruits of the living and the dead having become together, so that you may rule over both the dead and the living, all the dead are bold, not by word, the flock.",
    "“Receive then my spirit.”",
    "Do not permit your sparrow to be lured by those hunting or by those meeting at the gates of enemies to plunder my exile from the earth or to disturb my ascent into the heavens.",
    "But this one indeed offered a prayer for himself, while another again offered one for the people of the Jews: “Lord, do not set this sin upon them.”",
    "And…"
  ],
  "source_text": "ψυχαὶ τῶν δικαίων εἰσέρχονται· οὐκέτι τὰ ζοφερὰ τοῦ θανάτου χωρία τὰ τῶν\nζώντων παραλαμβάνει πνεύματα. Μετὰ σὲ τῶν ζώντων ἀπαρχὴν καὶ νεκρῶν ἅμα\n5\nγενόμενον, ἵνα καὶ νεκρῶν καὶ ζώντων κυριεύσῃς, ὅλων θαρρεῖ τῶν νεκρῶν, οὐκ\nἔξω λόγου, τὸ φύραμα. «∆έξαι τοίνυν τὸ πνεῦμά μου.» Μὴ συχωρήσῃς τὸ σὸν\nστρουθίον λοχῆσαι τοῖς θηρεύουσι μηδὲ τοῖς συναντῶσιν ἐν πύλαις ἐχθροῖς τὴν\nἐμὴν ἀπὸ τῆς γῆς ἀποδημίαν λυμαίνεσθαι μηδὲ θορυβῆσαί μοι τὴν εἰς οὐρανοὺς\nἄνοδον.\n27 Ἀλλὰ ταύτην μὲν ὑπὲρ ἑαυτοῦ τὴν προσευχήν, ἑτέραν δὲ πάλιν ὑπὲρ τοῦ\nλαοῦ τῶν Ἰουδαίων ἔθυεν· «Κύριε, μὴ στήσῃς αὐτοῖς τὴν ἁμαρτίαν ταύτην.» Καὶ",
